   "why": "The bad sample raises the gradient norm on the step it arrives. The loss on ordinary data cannot move until that gradient has been applied, so it peaks one step later. The gradient norm is a leading indicator and the loss is a lagging one \u2014 which is why the gradient norm is the thing worth alerting on."
